WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.128 --> 00:00:03.128
(missile whooshing)

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:06.870
- On Wednesday evening,

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:08.860
North Korea launched
two ballistic missiles

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:09.910
off its east coast

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:12.113
for the first time since March this year.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.660
North Korea state media released photos

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.010
and videos of the launch,

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:18.860
and it was conducted from a railway

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:20.840
in North Korea's central region.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:23.959
State media referred to them
as railway-borne missiles.

00:00:23.959 --> 00:00:27.580
We see in the footage that
a train slowly comes out

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:28.450
of the tunnel.

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:30.690
We see some people in hazmat suits

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:32.640
that come out preparing for the launch.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:34.390
The anchor in the video says

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:37.983
that the launch occurred
at dawn on September 15th.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:42.230
And this was the first
time that North Korea

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:45.993
was showing off its
railway-borne missile technology.

00:00:46.877 --> 00:00:49.710
(missile booming)

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:52.630
The missiles flew about 500 miles

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:54.550
at an altitude of 37 miles

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:56.070
before splashing into the waters

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.300
between Korea and Japan,

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.860
which has caused alarm for officials.

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:01.240
What's unique is that North Korea

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:02.910
has an extensive railway network,

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:04.000
and this means South Korean

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.270
and US officials now have to
track rail-launched missiles,

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:10.170
as well as road launchers and
submarine-launched missiles.

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:14.660
North Korea has kept quiet
for quite a long time

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:16.270
since the pandemic began.

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:19.230
North Korea has been consumed
by domestic problems.

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:22.340
It's kept its borders closed
largely due to COVID fears

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:25.500
and has admitted to food shortages.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.000
A lot of North Korea watchers say

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.130
that this recent missile launch indicates

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:31.680
that North Korea wants to
not only ramp up pressure

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:34.170
but also get the US to
pay attention to them,

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:36.007
and resume dialogue.

00:01:36.007 --> 00:01:37.970
(missile booming)

00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:40.170
Weapons tests are definitely
one of the methods

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:43.103
that North Korea uses to dial
up pressure on Washington.

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:46.280
Many experts that I've spoken to

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:49.521
have said that because the
US has been so consumed

00:01:49.521 --> 00:01:53.200
with Afghanistan and other
international matters,

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.850
this was sort of a chance for North Korea

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:57.011
to grab their attention
and say we're still here.

00:01:57.011 --> 00:01:59.360
We still have our weapons,

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:03.060
and we still have this
military power to show off.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.950
And they're basically hoping
to use that as leverage

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:08.443
once negotiations do eventually resume.

00:02:08.443 --> 00:02:11.443
(missile whooshing)

